{"version":1,"type":"session-summary","driving_event":"Issue #605 requires the owning Node to rebuild Timeline orchestration state from its durable journal. Inspection showed that ACP Session IDs were still recovered only from the separate backend JSON map, so a missing map could create a replacement Session.","decision":"Add a versioned, checksummed per-Timeline JSON-lines journal with replay epochs and strict tail recovery; sync Gnostic admissions and ACP updates before dependent dispatch or forwarding; reconstruct projections and ACP Session bindings from journal events, using the sidecar only when journaling is unavailable.","impact":"The journal becomes the authoritative durable Timeline record while the bounded Turn log remains digest-only. Serve and runner require configured durable state, ACP Session recovery no longer depends on its sidecar when the journal capability is present, and the v1 on-disk format is documented. No dependency was added.","recurrence_control":"Tests exercise write-before-dispatch, exact ACP update preservation, replay and corruption recovery, and Session recovery after deleting the backend map. make verify, make container-smoke, make runner-smoke, make acp-smoke, and git diff --check passed.","rejected_alternatives":["Treat the ACP backend JSON map as session authority; it can drift from or outlive the Timeline journal.","Reuse the prior Positronic transcript store; it is backend-owned and violates the v0.5 ownership boundary."],"sources":[]}
